WEBVTT

00:13.013 --> 00:15.015
[suspenseful music playing]

00:17.934 --> 00:19.102
[yells in pain]

00:29.863 --> 00:31.531
[suspenseful music continues]

00:31.614 --> 00:32.824
[distant rapid gunfire]

00:38.079 --> 00:40.165
- [gunshot]
- [grunts, groans]

00:42.500 --> 00:44.044
[straining]

00:44.544 --> 00:45.837
[Won-seong straining]

00:48.673 --> 00:50.300
This is your last warning.

00:50.383 --> 00:51.634
Drop the gun now.

00:51.718 --> 00:53.053
Ah! Okay! Okay!

00:53.553 --> 00:54.512
Here, okay?!

00:54.596 --> 00:55.430
Here's the gun!

00:56.347 --> 00:57.432
Captain, are you all right?

00:58.224 --> 00:59.893
[Joo groaning]

00:59.976 --> 01:01.227
Yes, Captain Joo is stable.

01:01.311 --> 01:03.313
[suspenseful music continues]

01:07.776 --> 01:10.111
[grunting]

01:13.073 --> 01:15.075
[Won-seong grunting]

01:15.784 --> 01:17.786
[Won-seong breathing heavily]

01:20.330 --> 01:22.332
[chuckling]

01:31.841 --> 01:34.010
- [Won-seong groans]
- [tense music playing]

01:39.057 --> 01:40.308
[music fades]

01:42.018 --> 01:44.979
[Do] This is your last warning.
Drop the gun now.

01:49.150 --> 01:50.151
That's…

01:51.611 --> 01:54.656
Wow. That's just so impressive.
I'm at a loss for words.

01:54.739 --> 01:56.908
How… What gave you
the courage to go in there?

01:56.991 --> 02:00.286
Oh, you know,
anything for a good scoop, right?

02:00.370 --> 02:02.622
You don't learn
that sort of thing overnight. [chuckles]

02:02.705 --> 02:05.500
Man, you've still got that edge, huh?
[chuckles]

02:06.084 --> 02:07.377
- Take a look.
- [man] Yeah?

02:08.086 --> 02:10.463
Have you ever seen a gun like that
in your life?

02:11.005 --> 02:12.215
[man] No, I haven't. Why?

02:13.842 --> 02:15.677
'Cause there's way more to see.

02:16.261 --> 02:17.762
The shooting at the gosiwon?

02:20.515 --> 02:22.142
There's a way bigger story here.

02:23.184 --> 02:26.437
And if there is,
bring me more exclusives like this one.

02:26.521 --> 02:27.814
And then what?

02:27.897 --> 02:30.316
[man] I'll do what I can to get you
a permanent position.

02:30.400 --> 02:31.901
No more freelance, huh?

02:31.985 --> 02:34.487
A real sense of belonging.
An office overlooking the mountain.

02:34.571 --> 02:36.114
What mountain is that?

02:36.197 --> 02:37.699
A panoramic view, okay?

02:38.783 --> 02:39.909
You telling the truth?

02:39.993 --> 02:42.579
- [laughs] A panoramic view.
- [chuckles]

02:44.497 --> 02:46.207
Goodbye, freelance.

02:47.292 --> 02:49.294
[intriguing music playing]

02:54.507 --> 02:56.134
[gun clicks, fires]

02:56.843 --> 02:57.927
[music fades]

03:03.683 --> 03:04.893
[woman on phone] Breaking news.

03:04.976 --> 03:07.562
A horrific shooting
occurred on November 21st,

03:07.645 --> 03:11.608
when a man cut off his ankle monitor
and headed to a nearby police station

03:11.691 --> 03:14.444
and randomly opened fire
at the officers present.

03:14.944 --> 03:16.112
He chose the station at night…

03:16.196 --> 03:17.155
ONE KILLED AT SCENE

03:17.238 --> 03:19.032
…knowing there would be
fewer officers on duty.

03:19.115 --> 03:21.034
- So cool.
- And they would mostly be unarmed.

03:21.534 --> 03:23.786
The shooter was shot
and killed by a police officer

03:23.870 --> 03:25.038
in the struggle that ensued,

03:25.622 --> 03:27.832
which is causing some controversy.

03:27.916 --> 03:29.918
[uneasy music playing]

03:30.501 --> 03:31.502
[phone keys tapping]

03:31.586 --> 03:33.087
PURCHASE A GUN

03:33.171 --> 03:34.714
WE'RE GIVING AWAY GUNS! FREE GUN

03:34.797 --> 03:36.799
[water boiling]

03:42.055 --> 03:43.348
[music fades]

03:43.431 --> 03:46.184
GYEONGIN SEOBU POLICE STATION

03:46.267 --> 03:48.269
[distant siren wailing]

03:51.940 --> 03:54.817
So you got the gun from the evidence room.

03:56.694 --> 03:59.155
Still doesn't explain
where the bullets are from.

03:59.739 --> 04:02.367
There were no bullets
recorded on the evidence list.

04:03.576 --> 04:06.621
They're bullets
you received from Mr. Moon Baek?

04:06.704 --> 04:08.873
He accompanied you to the scene, yes?

04:09.374 --> 04:11.960
You first encountered him
at Won-seong's residence?

04:12.043 --> 04:12.877
Yes.

04:12.961 --> 04:14.545
And what were you doing there?

04:14.629 --> 04:18.758
Well, I already, uh, told
the other guy all that.

04:19.884 --> 04:21.052
Or… Where did he go?

04:21.552 --> 04:23.054
Told who?

04:23.137 --> 04:24.347
[chuckles]

04:24.430 --> 04:25.431
Yeah. [tuts]

04:25.932 --> 04:28.851
How about I tell you the whole truth
from the beginning?

04:28.935 --> 04:32.063
Mr. Moon Baek said you took the bullets
he was to hand over to police.

04:32.146 --> 04:34.357
What's the exact relationship

04:35.316 --> 04:36.567
between you

04:37.485 --> 04:38.778
and Mr. Moon Baek?

04:39.988 --> 04:41.406
I met him by accident.

04:41.489 --> 04:43.116
And given the situation…

04:45.201 --> 04:46.035
asked for his help.

04:46.119 --> 04:47.203
[scoffs]

04:53.793 --> 04:57.463
Describe in your own words what happened
when you confronted Won-seong.

04:58.881 --> 05:00.925
Mr. Won-seong was desperate.

05:01.801 --> 05:04.804
He had shot his probation officers and was

05:06.014 --> 05:07.432
in a killing frenzy.

05:08.433 --> 05:10.685
I decided to stop him.
I had to act quickly.

05:11.185 --> 05:15.565
Even so, wasn't it a bit excessive…
to shoot him like that?

05:16.899 --> 05:18.359
[papers rustling]

05:19.736 --> 05:21.362
We looked at your record, Officer Lee,

05:21.863 --> 05:25.450
and it seems you volunteered
to be sent to high-risk conflict zones.

05:25.533 --> 05:28.286
- [uneasy music playing]
- Places everyone else shied away from.

05:29.746 --> 05:32.582
As of yesterday,
your body count was up to 99.

05:35.376 --> 05:37.712
After today, it's 100 people.

05:42.300 --> 05:44.052
What does that have to do with anything?

05:45.261 --> 05:48.306
Look…
why don't you just be honest with us?

05:51.309 --> 05:54.687
The truth is,
you wanted to kill them all, didn't you?

05:56.773 --> 05:58.274
Are you really asking me that?

05:58.358 --> 06:01.444
I'm asking because we have
a reason to be suspicious.

06:02.528 --> 06:03.571
[sighs]

06:07.200 --> 06:08.326
[music fades]

06:10.578 --> 06:11.454
Officer Lee,

06:12.080 --> 06:14.123
what are you doing in here?
Come on out now.

06:14.791 --> 06:17.251
Chief, we're holding an investigation.

06:17.335 --> 06:19.420
"Investigation." You damn parasites.

06:19.504 --> 06:21.172
Further investigation is needed

06:21.255 --> 06:23.633
to see if he used the gun
according to regulation.

06:23.716 --> 06:27.762
You saw the security footage.
He saved the lives of 30 of our men.

06:27.845 --> 06:30.598
He's the only one who ran in there
to try and save people.

06:30.681 --> 06:32.350
Didn't you see what he did last night?

06:32.433 --> 06:36.312
Whatever his reason, he used
illegal ammunition to fire that gun.

06:36.396 --> 06:39.023
So… we'll be reporting him.

06:39.107 --> 06:40.608
You do that.

06:41.734 --> 06:43.027
But if you're gonna stand around

06:43.111 --> 06:45.071
and discipline an officer
for doing his job,

06:45.154 --> 06:46.364
you should start with me.

06:46.447 --> 06:49.784
I'm his superior.
I gave the order. I'm the one in charge.

06:49.867 --> 06:51.369
I'm in charge here, damn it!

06:51.452 --> 06:53.996
Don't even think about
making him into a patsy!

06:54.080 --> 06:55.998
Wanna punish someone?
Start with me, you leeches!

06:56.082 --> 06:58.876
You'll be the first ones running
when the bullets are flying.

06:58.960 --> 07:00.795
So how dare you. [tuts]

07:01.504 --> 07:02.505
Come with me!

07:03.089 --> 07:04.841
INTERROGATION ROOM

07:08.719 --> 07:10.012
I'm sorry, sir.

07:10.096 --> 07:11.848
There's nothing to apologize for.

07:12.682 --> 07:15.476
We'll handle things from here,
so go home and get some rest.

07:16.894 --> 07:18.062
And keep your head up!

07:19.605 --> 07:20.815
[elevator dings]

07:20.898 --> 07:22.900
[distant siren wailing]

07:25.278 --> 07:27.280
[indistinct chatter]

07:35.163 --> 07:35.997
Lee Do!

07:36.080 --> 07:38.040
- Sergeant Cho.
- Are you all right?

07:43.171 --> 07:45.131
Officer Lee,
what happened to yesterday's shooter?

07:45.214 --> 07:46.382
[reporters shouting questions]

07:46.466 --> 07:48.718
We have nothing to say at the moment.
No comment.

07:49.510 --> 07:52.096
- Move aside. Move aside, please.
- [reporters shouting questions]

07:57.435 --> 07:58.978
You didn't have to come.

08:01.689 --> 08:02.773
[Cho sighs]

08:03.524 --> 08:06.569
From your grade school
to your university graduation,

08:06.652 --> 08:09.572
shooting competitions,
the military deployment overseas,

08:09.655 --> 08:10.698
police exam,

08:10.781 --> 08:13.242
is there a single one
that I wasn't there for?

08:15.661 --> 08:16.704
Yes or no?

08:17.955 --> 08:18.789
I'm sorry.

08:18.873 --> 08:21.417
It'd be nice
if you showed some appreciation for once.

08:21.501 --> 08:24.795
It hurts my feelings when the things
I do for you go unnoticed. [tuts]

08:25.546 --> 08:27.590
You didn't make it to all my competitions.

08:27.673 --> 08:30.426
[scoffs] You're lucky
I don't make you walk home.

08:34.597 --> 08:35.723
How is Se-yeong doing?

08:35.806 --> 08:38.184
See? See? Oh, sure. Change the subject

08:38.267 --> 08:40.311
just because you don't like
what we're discussing.

08:40.394 --> 08:43.606
Do you really think you should be
worrying about others right now?

08:43.689 --> 08:46.651
Don't worry about Se-yeong.
Worry about yourself.

08:48.277 --> 08:49.403
[exhales forcefully]

08:51.989 --> 08:54.116
Are you… okay?

08:54.992 --> 08:56.744
Don't I look okay?

08:56.827 --> 08:59.664
Come on, I'm not talking about your body.

09:00.957 --> 09:03.876
About picking up a gun again.
It must've been hard for you.

09:05.628 --> 09:08.464
Just don't get involved
if you don't have to, all right?

09:09.423 --> 09:11.801
I can't bear to see you get hurt again,

09:12.802 --> 09:14.303
physically or mentally.

09:15.471 --> 09:17.139
Probably not something a cop should say.

09:17.223 --> 09:19.058
Well, I'm nearly 60! I don't give a shit

09:19.141 --> 09:21.811
if people have a problem
with what I have to say.

09:21.894 --> 09:24.105
- I can say what I want, you prick.
- [laughs]

09:24.605 --> 09:26.107
Listen. I'm being serious.

09:26.190 --> 09:29.193
Do you know how worried I was
when I heard you picked up a gun?

09:29.277 --> 09:31.445
It broke my heart in pieces.

09:31.529 --> 09:33.531
- [Cho sighs]
- [somber music playing]

09:34.991 --> 09:37.827
[door mechanism beeping]

09:46.043 --> 09:48.045
[groans softly]

09:52.216 --> 09:54.969
[echoing] As of yesterday,
your body count was up to 99.

09:56.178 --> 09:58.264
After today, it's 100 people.

09:58.973 --> 10:01.809
[echoing] The truth is,
you wanted to kill them all, didn't you?

10:01.892 --> 10:03.185
[young Do whimpering]

10:03.269 --> 10:04.353
- [screams]
- [rapid heartbeat]

10:04.437 --> 10:05.479
[gunshot]

10:05.563 --> 10:07.356
[automatic gunfire echoing]

10:07.440 --> 10:09.442
[somber music continues]

10:11.277 --> 10:13.404
- [sighs]
- [music fades]

10:13.487 --> 10:16.240
- Don't be such a chicken, you little shit.
- [boy 2] Lard-ass is here.

10:16.324 --> 10:18.909
[boy 1] Get a move on, shithead!
For fuck's sake.

10:22.371 --> 10:23.414
[Seong-jun] Fatty,

10:25.166 --> 10:26.167
you a bully?

10:27.293 --> 10:28.544
[boy 3] Hey, fuck-face.

10:30.254 --> 10:31.422
[students murmuring]

10:32.882 --> 10:34.216
[boy 4] Is he crazy?

10:35.092 --> 10:36.427
[boy 5] What the hell?

10:36.510 --> 10:37.678
[breathing shakily]

10:38.554 --> 10:40.598
You better bring your mom's ID.

10:40.681 --> 10:43.601
- [boy 6] That's scary. Do we tell someone?
- S… s… stupid kid.

10:47.813 --> 10:49.982
[Cho] Yes, yes. I understand.

10:50.066 --> 10:52.026
DISCIPLINARY COMMITTEE DECISION

10:52.109 --> 10:53.319
But, you know, this is--

10:54.528 --> 10:57.448
Yes, a decision had to be made. Mm-hmm.

10:58.949 --> 11:01.452
Seriously? A three-month suspension?

11:02.119 --> 11:03.913
Isn't that a bit excessive?

11:04.580 --> 11:07.083
They really came down hard. [tuts]

11:07.166 --> 11:10.252
[Jeong-u] Do they even know
how many people Officer Lee saved?

11:12.296 --> 11:13.130
He's outside.

11:27.144 --> 11:28.104
Any chance

11:28.688 --> 11:31.899
there's more information
on that person from outside Won-seong's?

11:32.650 --> 11:34.443
Uh, I believe, um…

11:34.527 --> 11:37.738
Uh, Lee Do,
you can't really work on anything.

11:38.239 --> 11:42.243
[sighs] Come on, don't be so heartless,
for God's sake.

11:42.785 --> 11:45.705
Why, Officer Lee never said
he was going to do anything.

11:45.788 --> 11:48.040
He's just asking a question, isn't he?

11:48.124 --> 11:52.086
Doesn't everyone have a question or two
in their hearts they'd like answered, hmm?

11:53.879 --> 11:54.922
Actually,

11:55.715 --> 11:57.633
I've been curious about that myself.

11:57.717 --> 12:00.594
Officer Jang, brief me
on what happened with that man.

12:00.678 --> 12:02.847
For you,
I'm happy to give a rundown, Sergeant.

12:02.930 --> 12:05.015
Mm, the guy
who ran out of Won-seong's house.

12:05.099 --> 12:06.100
You find out who he was?

12:06.183 --> 12:07.309
He wasn't there.

12:07.393 --> 12:08.728
He wasn't? Why you little…

12:08.811 --> 12:10.980
You better tell the truth
or you'll also get suspended.

12:11.564 --> 12:13.107
I swear, he wasn't there.

12:13.190 --> 12:16.235
Wait. What do you mean he wasn't there?
You went immediately?

12:16.318 --> 12:18.112
Yes, Officer Lee asked you to hurry up.

12:18.195 --> 12:20.364
- Yes, and I got there really fast.
- And then?

12:20.448 --> 12:23.075
And then… there seemed to be a lot more.

12:24.785 --> 12:27.663
[Do] Give me the license plate number
of the vehicle and their route.

12:27.747 --> 12:31.500
Just tell me their license plate number.
And the route their vehicle took. Tell me.

12:31.584 --> 12:32.418
Okay.

12:32.501 --> 12:34.587
- Uh, we can't really see the route.
- [Cho] Okay.

12:34.670 --> 12:39.133
[Jeong-u] But the plate number was 1-5-N…
2-3 something…

12:39.216 --> 12:40.634
[suspenseful music playing]

12:42.762 --> 12:44.346
1-5-N 2-3-3-5.

12:45.055 --> 12:46.056
Oh! He's right.

12:46.140 --> 12:48.434
- Excuse me, let me check something.
- Okay.

12:51.437 --> 12:52.772
[officer] Wait a second…

12:53.564 --> 12:54.857
[inhales deeply]

12:55.816 --> 12:57.985
That looks like U-tae, doesn't it?

12:58.068 --> 13:00.738
Good work!
Yeah, I was thinking the same thing.

13:02.031 --> 13:03.157
Who's this U-tae?

13:03.240 --> 13:05.117
Oh, just some asshole.

13:05.201 --> 13:08.287
He's been causing problems
in the neighborhood for years.

13:09.580 --> 13:13.167
Now that I think of it,
didn't he just get out of prison recently?

13:13.250 --> 13:16.003
Yeah, right. I heard
he was spending the majority of his days

13:16.086 --> 13:17.838
doing gofer work for Manager Gong.

13:17.922 --> 13:21.425
By Manager Gong,
do you mean Seok-ho of the Glory Gang?

13:21.509 --> 13:23.677
Oh, right you are. Yeah.

13:23.761 --> 13:25.888
Didn't you once work with Detective Seo,

13:25.971 --> 13:28.015
trying to take down Manager Gong?

13:28.098 --> 13:30.684
- [music fades]
- Yeah, it's the same Gong Seok-ho.

13:31.811 --> 13:34.021
Okay, let's have a look.

13:35.231 --> 13:38.192
Today's horoscope for Gong Seok-ho.

13:38.776 --> 13:41.403
"A forgotten enemy will pay you a visit."

13:41.487 --> 13:43.531
"Be sure to be on your guard." [laughs]

13:44.406 --> 13:45.616
- [phone buzzing]
- Shit.

13:46.992 --> 13:48.035
Well, that's eerie.

13:48.118 --> 13:49.119
POLICE IN NAME ONLY

13:49.203 --> 13:51.121
That horoscope's fire.

13:53.332 --> 13:54.542
Smug bastard.

13:54.625 --> 13:57.753
Detective Seo, it's me.
Can you tell me where Seok-ho is?

13:57.837 --> 14:00.130
- Aren't you suspended?
- I won't do anything, I promise.

14:00.214 --> 14:02.508
Don't worry about it.
I'll call you if there's anything.

14:02.591 --> 14:03.676
All right.

14:04.218 --> 14:05.886
Oh, and that Moon Baek guy?

14:05.970 --> 14:07.221
His record is spotless.

14:07.721 --> 14:09.056
- Really?
- Mm-hmm.

14:09.765 --> 14:12.726
All right, send me Seok-Ho's location
as soon as you can.

14:12.810 --> 14:13.644
Bye.

14:15.646 --> 14:16.605
- Officer Lee.
- Yes?

14:16.689 --> 14:17.731
What you asked for.

14:18.232 --> 14:20.693
- Ooh, nice bike.
- Good work.

14:21.402 --> 14:23.362
- Can you do me a favor?
- Sure.

14:23.445 --> 14:26.740
Could you find out whatever you can
about this person right here?

14:28.826 --> 14:30.286
Certainly, sir. I'll do my best.

14:30.870 --> 14:32.204
- Be careful.
- Yeah.

14:32.288 --> 14:34.290
[suspenseful music playing]

14:40.421 --> 14:42.590
"Dongwol Industries. Moon Baek."

14:48.637 --> 14:50.723
[suspenseful music continues]

14:54.977 --> 14:55.811
Got him.

14:56.812 --> 14:57.646
Who are you?

14:59.648 --> 15:01.025
I'm looking for Seok-ho.

15:01.108 --> 15:03.694
You can't just stroll in here.
Take a walk.

15:04.612 --> 15:06.405
We have a man out here who is--

15:07.323 --> 15:08.324
Manager Gong.

15:08.407 --> 15:09.575
[music fades]

15:11.577 --> 15:14.496
Holy shit, man, that horoscope.

15:14.580 --> 15:16.707
[man 2] Who the hell is this?
Does he have a death wish?

15:16.790 --> 15:18.292
Hey. It's all right.

15:19.501 --> 15:21.712
Move out of the way, shithead. Let him in.

15:21.795 --> 15:23.797
Everyone, move! Get outta here.

15:23.881 --> 15:25.883
Let me talk to this man. Go on.

15:30.512 --> 15:31.680
God damn…

15:34.767 --> 15:35.643
Whoa.

15:36.226 --> 15:37.770
If looks could kill, huh?

15:39.647 --> 15:40.814
Well, Officer Lee,

15:41.482 --> 15:43.609
you should be
focusing on keeping your precinct safe.

15:43.692 --> 15:44.985
What are you doing here?

15:47.905 --> 15:49.073
Manager Gong.

15:51.116 --> 15:52.326
You dealing guns?

15:52.409 --> 15:53.410
Whoa!

15:54.244 --> 15:55.412
[laughs]

15:55.496 --> 15:57.957
Shit. Guns?!

15:58.874 --> 15:59.875
That's…

16:00.459 --> 16:03.295
that's the question
you want to barge into my office to ask?

16:04.380 --> 16:05.381
Answer me.

16:07.925 --> 16:09.551
Are you dealing guns?

16:09.635 --> 16:12.930
Uh, should we have your head checked
or what?

16:13.013 --> 16:16.183
Take a look.
Do these look like guns to you?

16:17.643 --> 16:20.187
Hey. Any of you playing with guns?

16:20.270 --> 16:21.188
[laughs]

16:21.271 --> 16:23.399
Seriously, even toy guns made for kids?

16:23.482 --> 16:25.150
[all] No, sir!

16:27.569 --> 16:28.529
You heard that?

16:36.078 --> 16:37.746
[uneasy music playing]

16:37.830 --> 16:39.164
[Do] Do you know this man?

16:42.292 --> 16:43.127
Not a clue.

16:46.213 --> 16:48.841
We know he's working for one
of the businesses you run.

16:48.924 --> 16:51.927
Do you realize how many guys
I have working around here?

16:52.011 --> 16:54.638
How am I supposed to know
what each of them is up to?

16:56.098 --> 16:57.224
You have no idea?

17:01.020 --> 17:03.480
And you have nothing to tell me
in relation to the guns?

17:04.064 --> 17:07.443
I don't know anything.
And I've got nothing to tell you.

17:09.778 --> 17:13.699
In that case, I'm gonna start
looking for every shred of evidence.

17:14.992 --> 17:16.577
And if I find you're lying,

17:17.911 --> 17:20.414
that you are actually dealing in guns…

17:22.541 --> 17:23.876
you know what I'll do to you?

17:26.545 --> 17:30.007
You and I
may come from different sides of the road,

17:30.674 --> 17:33.093
but we both know accusations are useless.

17:37.014 --> 17:38.057
[Seok-ho inhales sharply]

17:40.100 --> 17:41.101
[exhales forcefully]

17:41.769 --> 17:45.189
You'd better… be telling the truth.

17:47.441 --> 17:49.735
Just remember I warned you.

17:54.490 --> 17:55.991
[door opens]

17:56.575 --> 17:57.576
[door closes]

17:58.077 --> 17:59.286
[exhales deeply]

18:03.290 --> 18:04.458
Who the hell's this guy?

18:04.541 --> 18:06.335
I've never seen him before.

18:16.428 --> 18:19.389
Could you please tell me
if this person works here?

18:19.473 --> 18:21.642
TECHNICAL SALES MANAGER
MOON BAEK

18:21.725 --> 18:24.561
[man] I'm sorry, but we can't check that
for you right away.

18:24.645 --> 18:26.814
As an arms company, there are strict rules

18:26.897 --> 18:29.566
before we can supply
the personal information of our employees.

18:30.067 --> 18:31.151
[Jeong-u] Officer Lee…

18:31.235 --> 18:32.277
DONGJIN APARTMENTS

18:32.361 --> 18:35.197
…I found the address of Mr. Moon Baek.
He lives in the Dongjin Apartments.

18:36.323 --> 18:38.325
[intriguing music playing]

18:43.413 --> 18:44.623
[line ringing]

18:44.706 --> 18:45.541
[Moon Baek] Hello?

18:46.250 --> 18:47.459
Hey, it's Lee.

18:47.543 --> 18:50.254
- What's going on?
- You got a minute for me?

18:50.337 --> 18:52.965
A minute? Sure, of course I do.

18:53.048 --> 18:54.174
We need to talk.

19:02.933 --> 19:04.935
[intriguing music continues]

19:16.238 --> 19:17.197
That's it, that's it!

19:17.281 --> 19:18.949
- See how low your back is?
- [music fades]

19:19.032 --> 19:20.576
- Don't forget to breathe.
- [men grunting]

19:25.873 --> 19:27.457
Holy shit, man.

19:27.541 --> 19:30.252
These are guns
disguised as regular packages in the mail?

19:31.086 --> 19:32.754
That doesn't seem reckless to you?

19:33.505 --> 19:34.339
Why?

19:35.299 --> 19:37.509
It's super safe
and not the least bit suspicious.

19:37.593 --> 19:38.760
They're being smart.

19:38.844 --> 19:41.847
Have you ever seen anyone in Korea
steal another person's package?

19:41.930 --> 19:44.057
It's against every known rule!

19:44.141 --> 19:45.767
Do you have more details on these people?

19:47.853 --> 19:49.354
I don't know them very well.

19:49.897 --> 19:52.774
But I'll say this, man.
They are some scary cocksuckers!

19:53.358 --> 19:54.735
And how many guns were there?

19:55.986 --> 19:57.321
You have no idea how many.

19:57.863 --> 19:59.615
I'd say… ten truckloads.

19:59.698 --> 20:00.699
Ten truckloads?!

20:01.283 --> 20:04.411
Yeah.
But we brought… about a half a truck?

20:04.494 --> 20:05.746
How'd you get in touch?

20:05.829 --> 20:08.207
I don't. I just do what I'm told.

20:08.290 --> 20:10.334
And they only contact me
when they feel like it.

20:10.417 --> 20:12.211
- Give me your cell phone.
- [sighs]

20:12.294 --> 20:14.630
Seok-ho didn't let me keep
anything like that.

20:14.713 --> 20:17.299
- Can't even play games if I get bored.
- [sighs]

20:17.883 --> 20:20.177
Hey. Storage room, you check it?

20:21.011 --> 20:21.845
I couldn't get in.

20:21.929 --> 20:25.432
Okay. Maybe Seok-ho doesn't even know
what's behind that door.

20:26.266 --> 20:27.100
The note.

20:27.184 --> 20:29.686
[Jeong-man] We should be careful
until we know what we're doing,

20:29.770 --> 20:31.563
considering how our boys ran into a cop

20:31.647 --> 20:33.607
when they went to that gosiwon
that got shot up.

20:33.690 --> 20:34.691
Exactly!

20:35.442 --> 20:37.236
The fact that there was a cop there

20:37.319 --> 20:40.489
means there are definitely guns
at those addresses on that list, right?

20:40.572 --> 20:43.533
- [U-tae] Fuck.
- [Kim] Come on, guys. Think about it!

20:43.617 --> 20:45.786
- [Kim groans in annoyance]
- [phone buzzing]

20:49.373 --> 20:50.666
GONG SEOK-HO

20:50.749 --> 20:52.834
That fucking bitch-ass,
lame-dick cocksucker.

20:52.918 --> 20:54.211
Why's he calling you?

20:54.294 --> 20:55.128
Huh?

20:55.212 --> 20:56.338
[tense music playing]

20:56.421 --> 20:58.382
[line ringing]

20:58.465 --> 21:01.218
Come on, come on…

21:01.301 --> 21:04.346
[automated voice] The person
you are trying to reach is unavailable.

21:04.429 --> 21:05.764
Please try again later.

21:06.265 --> 21:07.140
[disconnect tone]

21:07.641 --> 21:09.851
Ah, you cheeky bastard.

21:12.771 --> 21:13.855
[Kim exhales forcefully]

21:15.732 --> 21:18.402
[U-tae] So? Why do you think
Manager Gong called you?

21:18.986 --> 21:20.028
You think he's on to us?

21:20.112 --> 21:21.154
Hey, Jeong-man.

21:21.238 --> 21:23.573
What the fuck are you hesitating for, huh?

21:24.491 --> 21:26.535
I was lucky enough
to be able to hide one gun.

21:26.618 --> 21:28.996
The day Seok-ho finds out
there are more in that storage room,

21:29.079 --> 21:30.747
we're all supremely fucked!

21:31.790 --> 21:33.625
Men, the time is now.

21:33.709 --> 21:35.794
Break into that room. Bring those guns!

21:40.340 --> 21:41.341
He's right.

21:43.427 --> 21:44.761
Let's take them now.

21:44.845 --> 21:47.264
- Good!
- Ah shit, man.

21:47.347 --> 21:49.850
Bring them all here.
Don't leave any behind.

21:50.600 --> 21:52.561
You gotta be quick. No time to waste!

21:53.186 --> 21:54.896
- It's gotta be now!
- Shit, let's go.

21:54.980 --> 21:56.648
Move it! Go, go, go!

21:56.732 --> 21:57.858
Let's do this!

21:57.941 --> 21:59.443
[U-tae] Guys! Time to go!

21:59.526 --> 22:01.695
- [man 1] Boys, we're leaving!
- [man 2] Come on, boys!

22:01.778 --> 22:04.489
[men yelling indistinctly]

22:06.116 --> 22:07.492
[music fades]

22:09.036 --> 22:10.495
[Mrs. Oh] Oh, look at that.

22:11.163 --> 22:13.498
Today's rice is cooked perfectly.
[chuckles]

22:15.667 --> 22:17.711
My gosh. That looks good.

22:19.921 --> 22:21.715
[somber music playing]

22:21.798 --> 22:23.258
LISTEN TO MY DEAD SON'S MESSAGE!

22:23.342 --> 22:24.926
APOLOGIZE!
BAN DANGEROUS OUTSOURCING

22:28.138 --> 22:29.056
Sir!

22:29.556 --> 22:31.266
Sir! Wait! Wait! I just…

22:31.975 --> 22:32.809
[Mrs. Oh yelling]

22:32.893 --> 22:34.644
I thought you were gonna take care of her.

22:35.270 --> 22:36.396
That's all I want!

22:36.480 --> 22:38.148
Why's that so hard to do? Sir!

22:43.528 --> 22:45.530
[somber music continues]

22:52.037 --> 22:54.498
Whoa! Why is the floor
so slippery around here?

22:54.581 --> 22:56.166
- [boy 1] Oh no, you okay?
- [boy 2] Oh man.

22:56.249 --> 22:57.084
So messy.

22:57.167 --> 22:59.336
[boy 1] Why does this kid always drink
with his head?

22:59.419 --> 23:00.837
Wow. That looks delicious.

23:00.921 --> 23:02.923
[indistinct chatter]

23:08.595 --> 23:09.763
[sighs]

23:17.646 --> 23:18.688
[grunts]

23:19.523 --> 23:20.565
[groans]

23:23.902 --> 23:25.904
[somber music continues]

23:37.374 --> 23:39.209
[boy 1] Hey, Fuck-gyu!
You're not picking up?

23:39.292 --> 23:41.461
- [boy 2] Did he finally off himself?
- [boy 3] Fuck-gyu.

23:41.545 --> 23:44.339
- Can we visit your mom's restaurant?
- [boy 2] Making Fuck-gyu an orphan?

23:44.423 --> 23:46.925
- [Seong-jun] Is it true he's a bastard?
- [boy 2] You didn't know?

23:47.008 --> 23:48.802
[Seong-jun] So that's why
he's such a dumbass.

23:48.885 --> 23:51.805
- [boy 2] I feel sorry for your mom…
- [boy 3] Hey, why aren't you responding?

23:51.888 --> 23:55.058
[boy 2] Fuck-gyu, the minute you show up,
you're dead, you stupid loser.

23:55.934 --> 23:57.769
[exhales deeply]

23:59.312 --> 24:02.858
- [somber music continues]
- [breathing deeply]

24:07.779 --> 24:08.864
[Gyu-jin] Shit.

24:09.823 --> 24:11.032
- [man] Excuse me.
- [music stops]

24:11.116 --> 24:12.659
Do you live in Unit 1311?

24:24.588 --> 24:26.590
[mysterious music playing]

24:42.439 --> 24:44.441
[unsettling music playing]

24:57.287 --> 24:59.539
- [music fades]
- [melodic pop music playing]

25:07.297 --> 25:09.216
You're here. Want some?

25:13.470 --> 25:14.596
[Do sighs]

25:20.185 --> 25:22.437
What did you do at Dongwol Industries?

25:25.315 --> 25:28.777
Well, I was designing
and testing new ammo.

25:30.654 --> 25:32.822
Did you know… South Korea,

25:32.906 --> 25:37.494
a country practically devoid of firearms,
is actually the biggest bullet exporter?

25:37.577 --> 25:39.329
[laughs softly] Isn't that ironic?

25:41.873 --> 25:42.874
[laughs softly]

25:43.458 --> 25:44.543
[Do sighs]

25:45.835 --> 25:48.338
What were you planning to do
with the gun you got?

25:50.966 --> 25:52.008
About that…

25:53.510 --> 25:54.761
You really wanna know?

26:07.440 --> 26:08.441
All right.

26:10.777 --> 26:13.488
I have cancer. I'm dead in six months.

26:14.531 --> 26:15.740
Or maybe sooner.

26:17.409 --> 26:18.618
You don't believe me?

26:21.580 --> 26:22.664
[sighs]

26:24.332 --> 26:25.166
Look.

26:26.084 --> 26:27.669
They cut me open three times.

26:28.545 --> 26:32.090
It's in my blood now
and spreading all over.

26:33.258 --> 26:35.510
At first, Seoul.

26:37.053 --> 26:38.680
Next, Busan.

26:39.472 --> 26:41.725
From Busan… to Gwangju.

26:44.519 --> 26:45.687
[Moon Baek laughs softly]

26:46.730 --> 26:48.231
This thing called cancer.

26:49.816 --> 26:51.693
[sighs] You know, it…

26:52.902 --> 26:54.070
it hurts like hell.

26:55.488 --> 26:59.117
So… I was gonna bang!

26:59.200 --> 27:00.535
End it with fireworks.

27:01.578 --> 27:02.746
[sighs]

27:07.834 --> 27:09.794
But all you had were bullets.

27:10.545 --> 27:12.088
Without a gun, they were useless.

27:12.172 --> 27:15.967
I was checking out handmade stuff,
but they didn't really pique my interest

27:16.051 --> 27:19.137
until this strange little website
popped out of nowhere.

27:19.846 --> 27:21.473
It said they were giving out free guns.

27:21.556 --> 27:24.309
So I thought I would click on it
just to see what would happen.

27:24.392 --> 27:26.686
PRESS HERE IF YOU WANT A GUN

27:26.770 --> 27:29.481
Then, two or three days later,

27:29.564 --> 27:30.982
I received a package.

27:32.025 --> 27:34.694
But the annoying thing was
there were no guns in there.

27:34.778 --> 27:37.906
Just a piece of paper
and a bunch of bullets.

27:37.989 --> 27:39.991
[mysterious music playing]

27:40.825 --> 27:43.036
Try going back to that website.

27:44.120 --> 27:45.121
[sighs]

27:45.830 --> 27:47.874
I'd like to do that as well.

27:50.460 --> 27:52.295
See? Impossible.

27:53.254 --> 27:54.673
The website's gone.

27:54.756 --> 27:56.132
CANNOT CONNECT TO THE WEBSITE

27:57.050 --> 28:01.137
So I looked at the piece of paper
that came with the package,

28:01.638 --> 28:04.724
and it had the addresses
of people who had received guns.

28:05.225 --> 28:07.977
So I took it upon myself to visit one.

28:08.061 --> 28:11.189
Just in case there was a gun there.
What do you think I found?

28:12.941 --> 28:14.693
Where's that list of addresses now?

28:16.444 --> 28:17.904
I think I threw it out.

28:19.447 --> 28:20.448
I got rid of it.

28:20.949 --> 28:22.325
You expect me to believe that?

28:22.409 --> 28:25.161
Don't worry. I have a really good memory.

28:25.245 --> 28:27.372
It's all up here. [laughs]

28:28.498 --> 28:29.332
Yeah?

28:31.960 --> 28:34.170
If your memory's so good,

28:35.422 --> 28:37.048
those addresses in your head…

28:41.010 --> 28:42.637
write them all down here.

28:43.680 --> 28:44.681
[sighs]

28:44.764 --> 28:46.141
Yes, Officer.

28:50.395 --> 28:52.397
[mysterious music continues]

29:00.238 --> 29:04.284
DOMYEONG-RO 1-GIL, DONGAN-GU, GYEONGIN

29:07.746 --> 29:08.955
[uneasy music playing]

29:09.038 --> 29:09.873
What is it?

29:09.956 --> 29:11.583
You sure these addresses are right?

29:13.793 --> 29:14.794
'Course.

29:18.006 --> 29:19.549
- [music intensifies]
- Hey!

29:20.216 --> 29:22.218
Where are you going?! Jeez!

29:22.719 --> 29:23.720
[line ringing]

29:23.803 --> 29:26.264
MRS. OH

29:26.890 --> 29:29.476
[automated voice] The person
you are trying to reach is unavailable.

29:29.559 --> 29:30.518
Leave a message.

29:33.938 --> 29:35.356
[Moon Baek] Yeah…

29:36.566 --> 29:38.401
Where do we go from here?

29:40.320 --> 29:41.946
- [man 1] God…
- [man 2] Sir, sir!

29:42.030 --> 29:43.615
How long do I have to avoid these people?

29:43.698 --> 29:44.866
WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS ARE MURDER

29:44.949 --> 29:47.285
- [protesters yelling]
- Is it so hard to just get rid of them?

29:47.368 --> 29:49.204
[man 3] They're not doing
anything illegal.

29:49.287 --> 29:51.456
I'll… I'll do my best
to get rid of them, sir.

29:53.166 --> 29:55.043
- [tires screech]
- [music fades]

29:55.126 --> 29:56.461
- I'm so sorry, sir.
- [man 1 groans]

29:57.045 --> 29:58.421
Try to drive properly.

29:58.505 --> 30:00.548
- Sorry, she just popped out of the blue.
- Hmm?

30:00.632 --> 30:03.134
Please, sir. Get out of the car.

30:03.218 --> 30:04.552
I just wanna talk.

30:05.220 --> 30:06.054
Who is that?

30:06.763 --> 30:08.306
Have you lost your mind, lady?

30:08.807 --> 30:11.476
What do you think you're doing?
Out of the way!

30:11.559 --> 30:14.062
Is it so hard to offer
a few words of apology?

30:14.145 --> 30:15.605
I just need to talk to you!

30:15.688 --> 30:16.564
What should I do?

30:16.648 --> 30:18.983
What do you think? Just keep driving.

30:19.067 --> 30:21.236
- Keep driving?
- [man 1] You want me to do it?

30:21.736 --> 30:23.321
- Go, you bastard!
- [tires screech]

30:23.404 --> 30:25.281
Come on! Step on the gas!

30:25.365 --> 30:26.491
Go, go, go!

30:26.574 --> 30:27.700
[engine revs]

30:27.784 --> 30:28.868
[yelps]

30:28.952 --> 30:30.078
Why'd you stop?

30:30.161 --> 30:32.747
- Ma'am, please--
- Do your damn job for a change!

30:32.831 --> 30:34.040
- [tires screech]
- [yelps]

30:34.749 --> 30:36.626
- [engine revs]
- [tires screech]

30:37.126 --> 30:37.961
[passenger] Go!

30:39.462 --> 30:42.632
- [driver breathing shakily]
- What's she taking out of her jacket?

30:42.715 --> 30:45.009
- [driver] It's… it's a gun.
- Huh?

30:45.093 --> 30:46.344
- [gun clicks]
- [driver] Uh, sir…

30:46.427 --> 30:48.137
[laughs] Look how crazy she is.

30:48.221 --> 30:50.223
[somber music playing]

30:57.355 --> 30:58.690
[door opens]

31:00.233 --> 31:01.276
[door closes]

31:02.068 --> 31:03.361
[Mrs. Oh] What's this?

31:04.737 --> 31:05.572
[grunts]

31:11.661 --> 31:13.663
[somber music continues]

31:16.332 --> 31:18.167
ORDERER ADDRESS LIST
INFORMATION

31:18.251 --> 31:19.085
OH KYEONG-SUK

31:19.919 --> 31:21.296
[menacing musical sting]

31:26.759 --> 31:29.971
- [grunts]
- Holy shit! Get out of the car, sir!

31:30.054 --> 31:31.764
[man 2] Ji-woong! Ji-woong!

31:31.848 --> 31:33.433
- Where are you going?!
- [Kyeong-suk] Sir.

31:33.516 --> 31:35.518
- [tense music playing]
- [breathing heavily]

31:35.602 --> 31:38.104
You know who Min-ju is? I need to know.

31:38.187 --> 31:40.607
Who's Min-ju?
Who is that? I swear, I don't know!

31:40.690 --> 31:41.566
Oh!

31:41.649 --> 31:43.109
[gunfire]

31:46.237 --> 31:48.573
- [man 2 grunts, groans]
- [groans]

31:51.034 --> 31:52.619
- [man 2 groans]
- Are you lying?

31:53.202 --> 31:54.287
Do you not know?

31:54.996 --> 31:56.831
- How could you…
- [man 2 groaning]

31:56.915 --> 31:59.167
…how could you not know who Min-ju is?

31:59.918 --> 32:01.878
- That's not right.
- [man 2] I don't…

32:01.961 --> 32:05.798
- You, of all people.
- Please! I'm telling the truth, I promise!

32:05.882 --> 32:07.675
I don't know a Min-ju!

32:08.301 --> 32:10.720
He was an employee of yours.
Remember that?

32:11.387 --> 32:15.183
- [man 2 groans]
- He's my son… who's not here anymore.

32:16.100 --> 32:17.810
His body was torn in two

32:18.603 --> 32:22.565
because you overworked him
in order to save money.

32:23.566 --> 32:24.609
[groans]

32:24.692 --> 32:25.860
Oh God!

32:26.361 --> 32:29.197
I've been screaming his name
at the top of my lungs.

32:31.157 --> 32:33.201
What a joke we must've been to you.

32:34.160 --> 32:36.746
How easy it is to let us die like animals.

32:37.747 --> 32:41.709
And you… can't even remember
my dead son's name!

32:41.793 --> 32:43.044
[screams]

32:43.127 --> 32:46.255
Don't kill me, please! I didn't know.

32:46.339 --> 32:48.424
I'm… I'm begging you.

32:50.093 --> 32:53.471
Please don't kill me.
I'm sorry. [sniffles]

32:54.806 --> 32:57.892
Please, I'm begging you.
I'm so sorry, ma'am.

32:57.976 --> 32:59.978
[tense music continues]

33:00.603 --> 33:02.146
Save your apology…

33:05.274 --> 33:07.318
and give it to my dead son instead.

33:17.537 --> 33:19.539
[music fades]

33:20.415 --> 33:22.417
[line ringing]

33:24.043 --> 33:26.421
[Do] Mrs. Oh,
why haven't you been answering your phone?

33:26.504 --> 33:27.797
[Kyeong-suk] Officer Lee.

33:28.464 --> 33:31.092
- [chuckles]
- [rapidly approaching footsteps]

33:31.175 --> 33:34.887
I finally got my apology today.

33:36.639 --> 33:37.765
[sighs]

33:38.391 --> 33:40.309
No matter how much I screamed,

33:40.977 --> 33:42.770
no one would listen to me.

33:43.813 --> 33:45.815
To think he'd only talk to me

33:46.774 --> 33:48.568
as soon as I had a gun in my hand.

33:49.444 --> 33:50.278
Mrs. Oh.

33:50.361 --> 33:51.696
Yes, I know.

33:51.779 --> 33:53.948
[somber music playing]

33:54.032 --> 33:55.324
What I did was wrong.

33:55.408 --> 33:56.409
[sniffles]

33:56.993 --> 34:00.163
And now… that I got my apology,

34:01.956 --> 34:03.875
I should pay for what I did too.

34:05.585 --> 34:06.627
Officer Lee,

34:07.712 --> 34:11.174
please… let me cook a meal for my son

34:12.050 --> 34:13.634
one last time.

34:26.689 --> 34:27.815
Min-ju,

34:28.941 --> 34:30.151
you eat up now.

34:30.234 --> 34:32.153
[somber music continues]

34:32.236 --> 34:34.363
I finally got him to apologize.

34:35.114 --> 34:36.032
We did it.

34:38.409 --> 34:39.368
I don't think…

34:39.869 --> 34:41.704
[sniffles, laughs softly]

34:43.289 --> 34:46.042
…I'll be able to cook anything for you
for a while.

34:49.295 --> 34:50.379
[sniffles]

34:50.463 --> 34:51.881
I love you, son.

34:55.843 --> 34:57.136
[knock at door]

34:58.346 --> 34:59.514
[knock at door]

35:02.975 --> 35:04.811
Officer Lee, you came for me.

35:07.063 --> 35:08.106
[sniffles]

35:11.692 --> 35:15.113
- [music fades]
- [dogs barking]

35:17.740 --> 35:18.783
Who are you?

35:19.283 --> 35:20.535
Evening, ma'am.

35:21.160 --> 35:23.204
- Yes?
- [unsettling music playing]

35:23.287 --> 35:24.580
Tell me where the gun is.

35:25.414 --> 35:27.083
[distant siren wailing]

35:32.421 --> 35:33.714
[tires screech]

35:39.178 --> 35:41.430
What? You know that car?

35:41.514 --> 35:43.724
- [unsettling music continues]
- Just keep an eye on it.

35:49.564 --> 35:51.566
[humming]

36:01.367 --> 36:02.910
[music fades]

36:07.081 --> 36:08.332
[uneasy music playing]

36:19.427 --> 36:21.179
[door rattles]

36:21.679 --> 36:22.763
MRS. OH

36:22.847 --> 36:24.390
[line ringing]

36:25.975 --> 36:27.977
[phone ringing inside]

36:29.604 --> 36:31.063
[line ringing]

36:31.147 --> 36:32.732
[phone ringing inside]

36:35.401 --> 36:37.653
- [line ringing]
- [phone ringing inside]

36:43.534 --> 36:46.037
- [phone ringing]
- [line ringing]

36:51.042 --> 36:52.710
- [phone ringing]
- [line ringing]

36:56.005 --> 36:57.423
[phone ringing]

36:57.506 --> 36:58.549
OFFICER LEE DO

36:58.633 --> 36:59.675
[ringing stops]

36:59.759 --> 37:01.761
[tense music playing]

37:05.806 --> 37:07.475
[sighs deeply]

37:07.558 --> 37:10.353
The trick is to stay curious.

37:14.732 --> 37:17.693
LISTEN TO MY DEAD SON'S MESSAGE!

37:17.777 --> 37:20.363
[tense music continues]

37:21.322 --> 37:23.241
[music intensifies]

37:24.242 --> 37:25.660
[grunting]

37:29.247 --> 37:30.081
[groans]

37:32.792 --> 37:34.335
Who are we but our choices?

37:39.966 --> 37:41.968
[music intensifies]

37:43.344 --> 37:44.178
[music fades]

37:44.262 --> 37:46.305
- Fucking hell! What's going on?
- Shit! That scared me.

37:46.847 --> 37:48.474
- [man 1] Who's this guy?
- Shut your mouths!

37:48.557 --> 37:49.600
Sh, listen.

37:50.184 --> 37:52.061
Who told you
you were allowed to park here?

37:52.144 --> 37:53.521
[scoffs] Who the hell are you?

37:53.604 --> 37:55.147
Uh, Moon Baek.

37:55.231 --> 37:56.565
- Hey.
- The fuck you talking about?

37:56.649 --> 37:58.609
So why did you have to park
on this narrow road,

37:58.693 --> 38:00.987
knowing full well
no other cars could pass?

38:03.406 --> 38:05.074
[tense music playing]

38:05.157 --> 38:06.158
[laughs]

38:07.118 --> 38:11.080
Ah, we meet again,
you son of a bitch. [laughs]

38:16.085 --> 38:17.044
Smile.

38:17.128 --> 38:19.130
So I can take a picture for your funeral.

38:19.213 --> 38:20.172
Say kimchi.

38:21.007 --> 38:23.718
Okay. We got the message, so get lost.

38:24.635 --> 38:25.761
[incoming message alert]

38:25.845 --> 38:27.430
- [Chang-ju] Hmm?
- [man 2] Who is it?

38:27.513 --> 38:28.514
[man 3] Answer it.

38:29.140 --> 38:30.224
[man 4] Who the hell?

38:30.308 --> 38:31.517
[jaunty music playing]

38:31.600 --> 38:34.395
Back off! We got it already, so get lost!

38:34.478 --> 38:37.064
[mocking tone] Yeah, I got it.
So you guys can get lost too!

38:37.148 --> 38:38.524
- [man 1] Huh?
- [man 3] Guy's crazy.

38:38.607 --> 38:40.192
- Unless you wanna die.
- [man 1] What?!

38:40.276 --> 38:41.527
[Chang-ju] Hey! You asshole.

38:41.610 --> 38:44.572
- What the hell is that guy doing?
- That guy saw our faces. Is that okay?

38:44.655 --> 38:46.824
- [man 5 groans]
- Of course it's not! Get out of the car.

38:47.408 --> 38:48.242
[sighs]

38:48.326 --> 38:51.203
- [man 1] Wanna start something with us?
- This is about to get interesting.

38:51.829 --> 38:53.789
[man 1] You! Come here.

38:54.332 --> 38:56.959
- Where you going?
- [Chang-ju] Don't be a fucking asshole!

38:57.043 --> 38:59.337
- [man 1] How exactly are we gonna die?
- [man 4] Scared, huh?

39:00.254 --> 39:02.465
- He's running away.
- [man 5] I said come here, fucker!

39:02.548 --> 39:04.592
- [man 7] He's on something.
- [man 6] Outta the car!

39:04.675 --> 39:06.302
[men yelling aggressively]

39:06.385 --> 39:07.762
[engine roars]

39:07.845 --> 39:09.096
[man 2] Fuck!

39:09.180 --> 39:10.681
[men yelling aggressively]

39:10.765 --> 39:11.891
[man 7] Hey, hey!

39:12.391 --> 39:14.769
- [man 3] Don't let him go!
- [men yelling aggressively]

39:16.771 --> 39:18.230
[men yelling aggressively]

39:18.314 --> 39:19.982
- [tires screech]
- [man 3] Hey, hey!

39:21.942 --> 39:22.818
[music fades]

39:23.444 --> 39:25.738
- Where is she?
- [U-tae] Shut up!

39:25.821 --> 39:28.574
You're gonna die soon,
so I'd be scared if I were you. [laughs]

39:42.463 --> 39:44.006
Seok-ho send you here?

39:44.090 --> 39:47.093
Ah, he has no idea
what the hell he's dealing with.

39:47.593 --> 39:48.886
This is a real fucking gun.

39:48.969 --> 39:51.263
I pull this trigger,
you end up with a hole in your head---

39:51.347 --> 39:52.890
- [men exclaim]
- Whoa, holy shit!

39:52.973 --> 39:54.558
[dramatic music playing]

39:54.642 --> 39:55.684
Oh man.

39:56.185 --> 39:57.853
What a complete shit show.

40:00.439 --> 40:01.273
What?

40:01.774 --> 40:03.150
- What is it?
- [engine roars]

40:04.402 --> 40:05.444
The fuck?

40:05.528 --> 40:06.987
[chuckles]

40:10.449 --> 40:12.201
There's another car.

40:12.284 --> 40:14.328
[funky rock music playing]

40:28.134 --> 40:29.260
[man 1] Oh shit!

40:31.053 --> 40:32.555
[man 2] Get back. Careful.

40:33.889 --> 40:34.974
[men whimpering]

40:35.057 --> 40:35.933
[U-tae] Hey!

40:39.145 --> 40:40.980
- [man 3] Holy crap!
- [men whimpering]

40:41.647 --> 40:43.357
[man 4] I'm hit! I'm hit!

40:45.359 --> 40:46.610
[man 5] That was scary.

40:47.153 --> 40:49.280
You guys have no idea what blanks are?

40:49.864 --> 40:51.907
Let's smash him!

40:52.783 --> 40:55.286
[men screaming]

40:57.037 --> 40:57.997
[screams]

41:12.511 --> 41:14.472
Boys, let's go!

41:15.681 --> 41:17.224
[men breathing heavily, groaning]

41:21.020 --> 41:22.938
- [bone crunching]
- [yelling in pain]

41:23.022 --> 41:24.231
[funky rock music continues]

41:30.821 --> 41:32.031
- [phone ringing]
- That me?

41:32.531 --> 41:33.365
U-tae?

41:33.449 --> 41:34.992
[panting] Get in here, all of you.

41:37.661 --> 41:39.038
Grab your stuff and get inside.

41:39.121 --> 41:41.332
- Get ready for some heavy shit. Hurry!
- Let's do this!

41:42.458 --> 41:43.501
Come on, come on!

41:43.584 --> 41:45.711
Yeah, we got a call. Get in the house now.

41:46.295 --> 41:48.672
Let's go!
No time to waste assholes. Come on!

41:48.756 --> 41:49.840
Hurry! Hurry!

42:02.186 --> 42:03.312
Oh shit, man.

42:04.480 --> 42:06.190
[funky rock music continues]

42:11.737 --> 42:12.780
[music fades]

42:12.863 --> 42:13.697
You fucker!

42:16.575 --> 42:18.577
[men whimpering, groaning]

42:19.870 --> 42:21.121
[breathing shakily]

42:21.205 --> 42:23.207
[somber music playing]

42:26.418 --> 42:27.253
[Do] Mrs. Oh.

42:35.052 --> 42:36.971
I'll be back. Just hang in there.

42:41.517 --> 42:43.519
[menacing music playing]

42:45.104 --> 42:47.481
[men groaning]

42:51.151 --> 42:53.320
[music intensifies, fades]

42:53.404 --> 42:55.656
- [Chang-ju] What are you doing?!
- [vehicle approaching]

42:55.739 --> 42:57.825
- Stop acting like fools.
- They gave it to you.

42:57.908 --> 42:59.451
- [car horn honking]
- I just--

42:59.535 --> 43:00.494
Huh?

43:00.578 --> 43:01.829
[honks horn]

43:02.746 --> 43:05.416
- What the hell's he doing back here?
- I don't fucking know.

43:06.709 --> 43:08.085
[engine revs]

43:13.716 --> 43:14.592
[engine roars]

43:15.593 --> 43:16.802
[men exclaim]

43:18.554 --> 43:20.306
[tense music playing]

43:20.389 --> 43:22.933
Man, what a bunch of pussies.

43:23.017 --> 43:24.727
Fuck you!
I'll kill you, you son of a bitch!

43:24.810 --> 43:25.853
[man 3] Get the fuck back!

43:34.528 --> 43:35.487
[exhales sharply]

43:36.822 --> 43:38.824
[yelling in pain]

43:40.993 --> 43:42.119
Fucking shit!

43:43.078 --> 43:45.080
[choking, straining]

43:53.297 --> 43:54.214
[yelling]

43:57.593 --> 43:59.762
- [laughs]
- [man 5 yells]

44:01.639 --> 44:03.182
[tense music continues]

44:08.646 --> 44:10.147
[dramatic music playing]

44:16.904 --> 44:18.030
[man 2 groaning]

44:20.574 --> 44:21.867
[Moon Baek] Yeah? Take this!

44:22.618 --> 44:23.911
[men groaning]

44:27.414 --> 44:28.666
- [man 6] You!
- Ooh!

44:32.753 --> 44:35.756
- [Moon Baek] No! Let go of me!
- Where the hell is everyone?!

44:35.839 --> 44:38.342
- Where are you all?!
- Ah! Come on, man! Keep playing!

44:38.425 --> 44:40.135
[man 5] Out of my way, damn it!

44:43.222 --> 44:45.849
- [dramatic music continues]
- I got him! I got him!

44:51.563 --> 44:53.482
Now… sit back!

44:53.565 --> 44:55.734
- [man 4] Cocksucker!
- Stop holding me!

44:55.818 --> 44:58.696
You gang are
the biggest losers I’ve ever seen!

45:01.657 --> 45:03.242
[groaning, straining]

45:03.325 --> 45:04.743
[Moon Baek yells aggressively]

45:06.245 --> 45:07.121
[groans]

45:10.582 --> 45:11.917
[laughing]

45:14.002 --> 45:16.004
[dramatic music continues]

45:17.214 --> 45:18.257
[groans] Oh!

45:21.051 --> 45:24.972
This… is why… you don't…

45:25.055 --> 45:26.098
[music fades]

45:26.181 --> 45:27.766
…park here!

45:28.475 --> 45:31.729
- [men groaning, whimpering]
- [breathing heavily]

45:35.733 --> 45:38.318
[men groaning, whimpering]

45:38.402 --> 45:39.278
[screams]

45:39.361 --> 45:40.612
I'll kill you!

45:43.699 --> 45:44.992
Oh shit, man!

45:50.497 --> 45:52.291
[yelling in pain]

45:54.293 --> 45:56.295
[groaning, coughing]

45:57.045 --> 45:58.172
Let me go, shitbag!

45:58.255 --> 46:01.258
I promise you,
once I get my hands on you, you're dead!

46:01.341 --> 46:02.634
I'll have your ass for this!

46:02.718 --> 46:04.720
- [bone crunches]
- [screaming]

46:04.803 --> 46:07.097
- [door opens]
- [rapidly approaching footsteps]

46:07.806 --> 46:09.308
What the fuck's going on?!

46:09.850 --> 46:12.186
- [door closes]
- Oh shit. What the hell is this?!

46:12.269 --> 46:14.646
[menacing music playing]

46:14.730 --> 46:17.524
[men groaning]

46:17.608 --> 46:19.151
- [man screams]
- [music fades]

46:19.735 --> 46:21.737
[man groaning]

46:24.573 --> 46:25.866
[car approaching]

46:29.536 --> 46:31.914
- Who's that? Is she hurt?
- Open the door for me.

46:33.207 --> 46:34.666
[Kyeong-suk groaning]

46:39.338 --> 46:41.340
Press here to stop the bleeding.
I'll do the driving.

46:41.423 --> 46:42.424
Okay.

46:48.555 --> 46:49.556
[engine revs]

46:54.728 --> 46:56.146
[tires screech]

46:56.230 --> 46:58.232
[somber music playing]

47:03.403 --> 47:05.405
[breathing shakily]

47:06.281 --> 47:07.825
[Kyeong-suk gags, groans]

47:08.492 --> 47:10.077
[Do] You'll be fine, Mrs. Oh.

47:10.661 --> 47:12.913
Hold on just a little bit longer.
Just a little longer.

47:12.996 --> 47:14.414
Everything will be okay.

47:14.498 --> 47:16.750
We're almost there. Almost there.

47:17.960 --> 47:20.546
[man] About six minutes ago,
he turned right on Geumseong-ro.

47:20.629 --> 47:22.005
[woman] Uh, no, he turned left.

47:22.089 --> 47:23.465
Stop, stop. That was 96.

47:23.549 --> 47:25.342
- [somber music continues]
- [tires screech]

47:25.425 --> 47:26.260
SECURITY CAMERA CONTROL ROOM

47:26.343 --> 47:27.427
MRS. OH.

47:28.053 --> 47:29.263
I'm gonna put you on hold.

47:31.139 --> 47:34.643
Mrs. Oh, I'm dealing with something urgent
right now. Do you mind if I call you back?

47:34.726 --> 47:37.229
Oh, I see. I'm sorry to interrupt.

47:39.606 --> 47:40.816
I'm back. Go ahead.

47:41.775 --> 47:43.777
[breathing shakily]

47:49.867 --> 47:51.368
[breathing weakly]

47:54.413 --> 47:55.372
[murmurs]

48:02.629 --> 48:03.589
[tires screech]

48:06.258 --> 48:07.593
- [Do] Mrs. Oh.
- [groans]

48:08.093 --> 48:09.928
[Moon Baek] Careful. Watch her head.

48:11.680 --> 48:13.640
[Do] Mrs. Oh, you'll be all right.

48:13.724 --> 48:15.517
- Stay strong for a while longer.
- [coughing]

48:15.601 --> 48:16.476
Mrs. Oh.

48:17.269 --> 48:18.520
You need to stay awake.

48:19.021 --> 48:21.982
You need to stay awake, okay?
Everything will be fine. [echoing]

48:25.527 --> 48:27.529
[somber music continues]

48:38.332 --> 48:39.499
OPERATION ROOM

48:49.635 --> 48:51.637
[somber music continues]

49:28.465 --> 49:30.384
[music fades]

49:30.467 --> 49:32.469
[dramatic music playing]

51:46.728 --> 51:47.771
[music fades]

51:47.854 --> 51:49.856
[suspenseful guitar music playing]

52:42.534 --> 52:44.536
[music fades]
